{"nodes": [{"id": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "label": "Global CLAUDE.md operating guide (deploy target)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 1-10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds values, constraints and format for every project while process (task classification, risk tiers, verification, orchestration, completion gates) is deliberately delegated to Conductor, keeping one source of truth per concern."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_conductor_priority", "label": "Priority rule: CLAUDE.md never overrides a Conductor gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 7-10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Minimum ceremony' is declared a reporting principle, not permission to skip a check, because a values file is the most likely place a gate would be argued away; an override requires an explicit user message in the current conversation, and standing instructions do not qualify."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_production_first", "label": "Quality bar: production-first", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 14-21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No MVPs or prototypes: simplification is allowed only as a conscious architectural decision, never as a cut in reliability, and when there is no time or information to make it production-grade the correct output is a BLOCKED report rather than a draft dressed as done."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_code_integrity", "label": "Code integrity (no stubs, no elisions)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 23-31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Omissions and markers like // TODO or // unchanged are classified as defects rather than shorthand, since they are the form in which incomplete work most often passes review."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_module_size_signal", "label": "Module size: a signal, not a blocker", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 27-31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Targets ~200 lines (300 for Rust/Go/C++/C#) but explicitly refuses to let legacy files over 300 lines block a targeted edit, because forcibly fragmenting cohesive code is itself an antipattern; naming rules ban utils/helpers/misc so a file name states a responsibility."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_token_economy_rtk", "label": "Token economy with rtk (global guide)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 33-40", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same trade as the core body: shell reads pass through rtk's compression while Read/Grep/Glob bypass it, and edits stay on Edit/Write because precision outranks token savings."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_security_antipattern_registry", "label": "Security antipattern registry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 42-55", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A forbidden/correct table covering sessions, token validation, SQL and shell injection, XSS, path traversal, secrets and crypto; generation is forbidden even on direct instruction, making it one of the few rules a user request cannot unlock."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_tests_and_logs", "label": "Tests and logs requirements", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 57-64", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Coverage scales with blast radius: branching pure functions get happy path plus two edge cases, security operations get 100% branch coverage plus a simulated attack, and API authorization needs both the 200 and the explicit 401/403. Silent catch blocks and console.log('error') are banned; payloads are scrubbed of PII and tokens."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_language_and_reply_style", "label": "Language and reply style", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 66-77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Visible thinking must stay in the reply language and must not drift into the language these instructions happen to be written in, since the user reads the thinking too; the comprehension test is whether a non-programmer would follow it."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_outcome_first", "label": "Outcome first (section 5.1)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 79-88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A short answer comes from selection, not compression: drop what does not change the reader's next step, but never degrade into fragments, abbreviations, arrow chains or professional slang. Clarity outranks brevity."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_report_after_long_run", "label": "Report after a long run (section 5.2)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 90-98", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written as a briefing rather than a continuation of the agent's working thread: result first, then the one or two things needed from the user, each introduced as new, because the accumulated vocabulary belongs to the agent and not to the reader."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_artifact_length", "label": "Length of written artifacts (section 5.3)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 100-103", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Documents match the task in length \u2014 no extra sections, repeated summaries, or padding for weight \u2014 because length is routinely mistaken for thoroughness."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_correcting_yourself", "label": "Correcting yourself (section 5.4)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 105-109", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Announce a correction only when the error changes the user's code, conclusions or decisions; a slip that changes nothing is fixed silently, so corrections keep their signal value."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_unified_summary", "label": "Unified summary block (Changed / Verified / Risks / Impact / Status)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 111-126", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Emitted only when the reply contained code; labels render in the reply language but the Status tokens stay verbatim, and their semantics \u2014 including what a missing verification forces \u2014 are owned by the Conductor gate rather than by this file."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_fact_over_mood", "label": "Fact over mood", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 128-134", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Disagreement, pressure and praise are explicitly classified as non-data, so the response to any of them is to re-read the source: defend structurally correct code with facts, fix a confirmed regression immediately."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude_graphify_skill", "label": "graphify skill trigger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 137-139", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wired into the global guide so that typing /graphify invokes the skill before anything else, turning any input into a knowledge graph."}], "edges": [{"source": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "target": "deploy_global_claude_conductor_priority", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 7-10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "target": "deploy_global_claude_production_first", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 14-21", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "target": "deploy_global_claude_code_integrity", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 23-31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "target": "deploy_global_claude_security_antipattern_registry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 42-55", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "target": "deploy_global_claude_tests_and_logs", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 57-64", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "target": "deploy_global_claude_unified_summary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 111-126", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_guide", "target": "deploy_global_claude_graphify_skill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 137-139", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_code_integrity", "target": "deploy_global_claude_module_size_signal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 27-31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_language_and_reply_style", "target": "deploy_global_claude_outcome_first", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 79-88", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_language_and_reply_style", "target": "deploy_global_claude_report_after_long_run", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 90-98", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_language_and_reply_style", "target": "deploy_global_claude_artifact_length", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 100-103", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_language_and_reply_style", "target": "deploy_global_claude_correcting_yourself", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 105-109", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_unified_summary", "target": "adapters_core_body_status_tokens", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 121-126", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "deploy_global_claude_conductor_priority", "target": "adapters_core_body_completion_gate", "relation": "references", "confi